This looks like a spinach salad with a small amount of broccoli, some pepper strips, and possibly a few bits of cheese or nuts. It sits on a square plate about 24 cm wide, and the pile covers roughly 10 by 14 cm. The spinach leaves are loosely stacked, so I estimate about 40 g of spinach, plus about 15 g of broccoli and other toppings, for roughly 55 g of food in total.

Spinach is about 23 kcal per 100 g, so 40 g gives roughly 10 kcal. The broccoli and other toppings add about 10 kcal. There may be a little dressing or oil, which I put at about 20 kcal. That brings the total to about 40 kcal. I'll round up slightly to allow for small toppings I can't identify.

